{%- doc -%}
Splits a rich text body into bands at each h2 and echoes them joined by a marker, so a caller can capture
the output and split on that marker instead of keeping its own copy of this.

A body renders as one flat run of siblings, so a background has nothing to attach to and no selector spans
a run of siblings. Bands are the markup that gives each stretch of the body something to paint.

The rule is subtle enough that two copies of it would drift. A subheading introduces the h2 below it, so it
belongs to the band that follows -- but only when it closes its band. Used as a label mid-section, several
to one heading, it has to stay where it is, or the break moves off the h2 and splits a section in half.

Blank bands are dropped, so the caller can rely on forloop.first and forloop.last.

@param {string} content - the rich text to split (required)
@param {string} [separator] - the marker placed between bands. Defaults to <!--prose-band-->
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign band_separator = separator | default: '<!--prose-band-->'
  assign subheading_marker = '<p class="subheading"'
  assign chunks = content | split: '<h2'
  assign carry = ''
  assign emitted = false
-%}

{%- for chunk in chunks -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign body = chunk

    unless forloop.first
      assign body = '<h2' | append: chunk
    endunless

    assign next_carry = ''
    assign parts = body | split: subheading_marker

    if parts.size > 1
      assign tail = parts | last
      assign tail_pieces = tail | split: '</p>'
      assign closes_band = false

      if tail_pieces.size == 1
        # The band ends on the subheading's own closing tag, with nothing after it at all
        assign closes_band = true
      elsif tail_pieces.size == 2
        assign after_close = tail_pieces[1] | strip

        if after_close == blank
          assign closes_band = true
        endif
      endif

      if closes_band
        assign next_carry = subheading_marker | append: tail
        assign body = body | remove_last: next_carry
      endif
    endif

    assign body = carry | append: body
    assign carry = next_carry
    assign trimmed = body | strip
  -%}

  {%- if trimmed != blank -%}
    {%- if emitted -%}{{ band_separator }}{%- endif -%}
    {{- body -}}
    {%- assign emitted = true -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
